# EduBridge UI Design Rules

Canonical docs: `docs/design/MASTER.md`. Read MASTER before inventing layout, color, or component choices.

## Theme (locked)

- **Light only.** Do not ship a dark-mode toggle or ThemeProvider that flips product chrome.
- Do not apply `class="dark"` for product theming. Existing `.dark` tokens in `packages/ui` are dormant.
- Marketing and app share the same `:root` tokens.

## Tokens and CSS ownership

- Change design tokens only in `packages/ui/src/styles/globals.css`.
- Use semantic classes (`bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`) — never ad-hoc hex / `bg-blue-500` for brand color in features.
- Follow the two-compilation Tailwind model in `TAILWIND_SHADCN_GUIDE.md`.
- Prefer `gap-*` over `space-y-*` / `space-x-*`; use `size-*` for equal dimensions; `cn()` for conditional classes.

## Library ladder

1. Compose `@repo/ui` (shadcn) first.
2. Add shadcn via `pnpm ui:add` into `packages/ui`.
3. AI chat / voice / streaming → `@repo/ai-ui` + CopilotKit slots themed to tokens (`docs/design/ai-surfaces.md`).
4. Aceternity (`@aceternity`) → **marketing / public landing only**. Never Background Beams, Spotlight, Glare, infinite marquees, or glassmorphism stacks inside `apps/web/features/**` tenant modules.
5. Icons: `lucide-react` only — no emoji-as-icons.

## Product shell and density

- Workspace UI sits under the unified shell (logo, module menu, active-module pill, search, profile).
- Cards are rare — only when they hold interaction; prefer flat sections + Separator in the shell.
- Motion is meaningful (150–300ms, transform/opacity); honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## AI surfaces

- AI summaries are first-class components (narrative above charts), not a glowing chat orb alone.
- Agents draft; humans approve; writes go through server actions — show Draft / Confirm UI.
- CopilotKit dock uses sidebar/muted tokens — composed contrast, not a second theme.

## Accessibility (minimum)

- Contrast ≥4.5:1 text; visible focus rings; ~44px touch targets.
- Visible labels (not placeholder-only); status not by color alone.
- Dialog/Sheet/Drawer need Titles; charts need a text summary.
- Checklist: `docs/design/accessibility.md`.

## Anti-patterns (reject)

- Purple-on-white / purple-indigo “AI” gradients as brand identity.
- Cream + terracotta + generic serif spa look.
- Dual light+dark as the default product offering.
- Local color systems inside feature folders.
- Unstyled default shadcn zinc left as “good enough” brand without token intent.
